# ⛔ SECRETS — MUST NEVER BE COMMITTED
#
# WHY THIS FILE EXISTS, AND WHY IT DID NOT UNTIL NOW
#   `void-anchor` had NO .gitignore at all, while its git remote is
#   https://github.com/0xxx0/0xxx0.github.io — a PUBLIC repository.
#   A non-empty `.env` (160 bytes) sat untracked and unignored, alongside
#   `scripts/set-hermes-telegram-token.py`. A single `git add -A` from any
#   session or subagent would have published live credentials to GitHub.
#
#   This file is ADDITIVE. It removes nothing and ignores nothing that was
#   previously tracked. If a path here was already tracked, `git rm --cached`
#   is a separate, deliberate act — not performed here.
#
#   Hermes invariant: secrets in .env, settings in config.yaml.

# --- credentials and env ---
.env
.env.*
!.env.example
*.env
*.pem
*.key
*.p12
*.pfx
*.asc
credentials*.json
secrets*.json
*token*.json
*secret*
auth.json
auth.lock

# --- provider / API keys in any form ---
*_api_key*
*apikey*
*.token
.openrouter
anthropic*.txt
openai*.txt

# --- token-handling scripts (they read secrets; they should not ship) ---
scripts/set-hermes-telegram-token.py
scripts/check_or_credits.py

# --- Hermes runtime state (machine-local, not source) ---
.hermes/
hermes-workspace/node_modules/
hermes-workspace/dist/
__pycache__/
*.pyc
.claude/
session-*.jsonl

# --- macOS and editor noise ---
.DS_Store
._*
.idea/
.vscode/
*.swp
*~

# --- large local material that is not repo content ---
# (the archive and backups are sources, not site assets — see PUBLISHING_BOUNDARY)
ChatGPT-Backup-*/
*.zip
*.dmg
*.pkg

# --- the reversible staging area: undecided files, not discards ---
# QUARANTINE != DELETE. This is 22 GB awaiting a human decision.
delete/crushed-*/
reclaimed-*/

# --- ADDED 2026-09-25 by kestrel after finding private data staged for a PUBLIC remote ---
# The existing rule only covered session-*.jsonl, which missed the files actually at
# risk. Anything under AXIS/work/**/cache/ is raw conversation text or source bytes.
# Nothing here was previously tracked-and-then-removed, except where noted below.
**/msgs.jsonl
**/cache/
**/_rescued-*/
**/*_user.tsv
**/candidates.tsv
**/*__raw/
# the extracted third-party research library: kept on disk, must not be published
AXIS/library/GLYPH-VIS-READING/*.pdf
AXIS/library/GLYPH-VIS-READING/*.docx
AXIS/library/GLYPH-VIS-READING/*.epub
# other agents' private/experimental trees
*_archives/
AXIS/work/**/quarantine/

# the staging pen holds a live VM disk and GBs of material — never commit its contents
delete/crushed-*/
delete/reclaimed-*/

# --- 2026-09-25: close the _archive/_archives plural gap ---
# The earlier rule was `*_archives/` (plural). `_archive/` (singular) is a different
# string and slipped through. Targeted by CONTENT TYPE rather than by directory, so
# legitimate tracked archives (ops-hub/wiki/_archive and friends) are NOT untracked.
**/_archive/*.jsonl
**/_archive/*.seed*
**/_archives/*.jsonl
**/_archive/*_user.tsv
**/_archive/*candidates*
